{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Third_Eye","to":"Third Eye"},{"from":"Heavy_Blade","to":"Heavy Blade"},{"from":"Deus_Ex_Machina","to":"Deus Ex Machina"},{"from":"Hello_World","to":"Hello World"},{"from":"Echo_Form","to":"Echo Form"},{"from":"Conjure_Blade","to":"Conjure Blade"},{"from":"The_Bomb","to":"The Bomb"},{"from":"Ascender's_Bane","to":"Ascender's Bane"},{"from":"Steam_Barrier","to":"Steam Barrier"}],"pages":{"1886":{"pageid":1886,"ns":0,"title":"Ascender's Bane","revisions":[{"revid":56422,"parentid":55627,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Ascender's Bane\n| Image       = Curse-AscendersBane.png\n| Color       = Colorless\n| Type        = Curse\n| Cost        = -2\n| NoUpgrade   = true\n| Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}. <br>{{KW|Ethereal}}. <br>Cannot be removed from your deck.\n| GivesToPlayer = Unplayable, Ethereal\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Unplayable}} {{Keyword Infobox|Ethereal}}\n{{C|Ascender's Bane}} is an {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} Card. It is {{KW|Ethereal}}, and cannot be '''removed''' from your deck or {{KW|Transform|Transformed}} by any means.\n\n== Obtaining Ascender's Bane ==\nOn {{Asc|10|Ascension 10}} and higher, runs begin with a copy of '''Ascender's Bane''' in your starting deck. As there is no way to remove the card, high Ascension runs must always contend with at least one {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} in the deck.\n\nAs there is no other way to obtain a copy, '''Ascender's Bane''' is the only piece of game content locked behind [[Ascension]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n{{KW|Ethereal}} causes '''Ascender's Bane''' to {{KW|Exhaust}} after your hand is discarded for the turn. If this causes you to draw from {{C|Dark Embrace}} or gain a card from {{R|Dead Branch}}, those cards will remain in your hand until your next turn.\n\n=== Synergies ===\nAs '''Ascender's Bane''' is a '''{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}''', it interacts with the following:\n* {{C|Fire Breathing}} will deal '''6(10)''' damage when it is drawn.\n* {{R|Du-Vu Doll}} will give you '''+1''' {{BD|Strength}} each combat.\n* {{R|Blue Candle}} can be used to {{KW|Exhaust}} it for 1 HP. \n** However, as '''Ascender's Bane''' generally '''Exhausts''' at end of turn anyway, this is only helpful in unusual circumstances. For instance, losing the '''HP''' can trigger {{R|Centennial Puzzle}} at will.\n* When added to the deck, it will be negated by {{R|Omamori}}, or gain you '''6 max HP''' if you have {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} and ''not'' Omamori. However, since you start the game with your original copy, the only way for this to happen is if you duplicate the original.\nAs Ascender's Bane is {{KW|Ethereal}}, it interacts with the following:\n* When it '''Exhausts''', {{C|Feel No Pain}} gains you {{KW|Block}}.\n* Similarly, {{C|Dark Embrace}} will draw you cards, and {{R|Dead Branch}} will generate a card to replace it. These cards will be kept in your hand until your next turn.\n* {{R|Charon's Ashes}} will deal damage to all enemies.\n* {{R|Strange Spoon}} only affects cards that {{KW|Exhaust}} when played, so it will never prevent '''Ascender's Bane''' from '''Exhausting''' (unless you are doing so with {{R|Blue Candle}}).\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Being {{KW|Ethereal}}, Ascender's Bane will {{KW|Exhaust}} if it is in your hand at end of turn, even if it is {{KW|Retain|Retained}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* If '''Ascender's Bane''' is discarded, you may end up drawing it again. This is sometimes the correct thing to do, but it does introduce a downside to {{C|Calculated Gamble}}, {{C|Storm of Steel}}, and {{C|Unload}}, which will all force you to discard it.\n** {{C|All-Out Attack}} may also sometimes discard it unnecessarily.\n* As {{C|Clash}} can only be played when all cards in your hand are {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, if it is drawn at the same time as '''Ascender's Bane''', it cannot be played.\n\n== Trivia ==\nDespite '''Ascender's Bane''''s in game text only saying it cannot be '''removed''', it also can't be '''Transformed'''. However it can be '''duplicated''' using {{E|Duplicator}} and {{R|Dolly's Mirror}}.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1896":{"pageid":1896,"ns":0,"title":"Barricade","revisions":[{"revid":56611,"parentid":56431,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Barricade\n| Image       = Red-Barricade.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 3\n| CostPlus    = 2\n| Description = {{KW|Block}} is not removed at the start of your turn.\n| GivesToPlayer = Barricade\n| PowerGives = Block\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Barricade\n| Image        = Icon Barricade.png\n| Description  = {{KW|Block}} is not removed at the beginning of your turn.\n| Type         = Buff\n| Stacks       = Does not stack\n| BetweenTurns = \n| Cap          = \n| InteractsWith = Block\n}}\n{{C|Barricade}} is a 3 (2 if upgraded) {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 1 {{BD|Barricade}}, which prevents your {{KW|Block}} from being removed in between turns. As {{BD|Barricade}} does not stack, copies of {{C|Barricade}} played after the first have no additional effect.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{BD|Barricade}} takes precedence over {{R|Calipers}}, effectively removing all effects of the relic.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes well with ways to build up block, most notably {{C|Entrench}}.\n* Can enable {{C|Body Slam}} to do more damage through building up {{KW|Block}} over multiple turns.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2029":{"pageid":2029,"ns":0,"title":"Choke","revisions":[{"revid":55692,"parentid":50499,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Choke\n|Image       = Green-Choke.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Deal 12 damage.<br>Whenever you play a card this turn, the enemy loses (3;5) HP.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Choked}}\n{{C|Choke}} is a 2 {{Icon|GE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 12 damage and applies 3 (5 if upgraded) {{BD|Choked}}, which makes that enemy lose that amount of HP whenever you play a card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{BD|Choked}} causes the target to lose HP directly. It does not deal damage, meaning it bypasses {{KW|Block}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Adding beta art for Bane, Charge Battery, Fission, Choke, Corpse Explosion, and Equilibrium.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 7: Setting Up All the Things'''\n** Blue Candle and Medical Kit should now work with Choke and Thousand Cuts.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1805":{"pageid":1805,"ns":0,"title":"Concentrate","revisions":[{"revid":56370,"parentid":55402,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Concentrate\n| Image       = Green-Concentrate.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 0\n| Description = Discard (3;2) cards.<br>Gain {{Icon|GE}} {{Icon|GE}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Discard, Energy\n}}\n{{C|Concentrate}} is a 0 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It makes you select 3 (2 if upgraded) cards in hand to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]]. If there are not enough cards in hand when this card is played, all remaining cards will be [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]]. It gives 2 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy'''.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Ice Cream}} ensures that the {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' gained can be useful, even if no cards are left in hand after playing {{C|Concentrate}}.\n* {{R|Unceasing Top}} synergizes very well with this card, as the {{Icon|GE}} Energy can still be useful immediately even if {{C|Concentrate}} empties your hand.\n\n* {{C|Concentrate}}'s [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] effect synergises with several [[Silent]] cards and relics: \n\n==== Cards ====\n* [[Keywords#Discard|Discarding]] {{C|Tactician}} or {{C|Reflex}} will immediately activate their effects.\n* {{C|Eviscerate}} is discounted by X {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' this turn, where X is the number of cards discarded.\n* {{C|Sneaky Strike}} will now refund 2 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' if also played this turn.\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Tough Bandages}} will grant 3 {{KW|Block}} per card [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]].\n* {{R|Tingsha}} will deal 3 damage to a random enemy per card [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]].\n* {{R|Hovering Kite}} will generate 1 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' if this is the first time a card has been [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]] this turn.\n\n=== Neutral === \n* {{C|Concentrate}} can also be used to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] cards with end-of-turn effects, like {{C|Burn}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}} such as {{C|Regret}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Concentrate card reworked.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2426":{"pageid":2426,"ns":0,"title":"Conclude","revisions":[{"revid":54856,"parentid":50658,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Conclude\n|Image       = Purple-Conclude.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (12;16) damage to ALL enemies.<br>End your turn.\n}}\n{{C|Conclude}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 12 (16 if upgraded) damage to '''ALL''' enemies, and then ends your turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Playing this card twice through an effect like {{C|Omniscience}} or a {{P|Duplication Potion}} will result in that effect being wasted, as the first copy played already ends your turn, preventing the second play.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2413":{"pageid":2413,"ns":0,"title":"Conjure Blade","revisions":[{"revid":56946,"parentid":53292,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Conjure Blade\n|Image       = Purple-ConjureBlade.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = -1\n|Description = Shuffle an {{C|Expunger}}(; with X+1) into your draw pile. <br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n}}\n{{C|Conjure Blade}} is an X {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It shuffles an {{C|Expunger}} into your draw pile, which deals 9 (15 if upgraded) damage X (X+1 if {{C|Conjure Blade}} was upgraded) times. This means it is possible to generate an {{C|Expunger}} that deals damage 0 times. {{C|Conjure Blade}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\nWhen playing an X {{Icon|PE}}-cost card, all {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' that you currently have will be consumed. The {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' consumed this way will be used as the value for X.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* If you have played {{C|Master Reality}} before playing this card, it will shuffle an upgraded {{C|Expunger}} into your draw pile instead.\n* {{R|Chemical X}} makes the X of the {{C|Expunger}} generated by {{C|Conjure Blade}} increase by 2, regardless of the amount of {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' used to play {{C|Conjure Blade}}.\n* If played using {{P|Distilled Chaos}}, {{C|Havoc}}, or {{C|Omniscience}}, it will play for the full current {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' without actually using any.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If {{C|Conjure Blade}} is duplicated with an effect such as a {{P|Duplication Potion}} or {{C|Burst}}, the value of X will also be used for the copy.\n* Being an X-cost, {{C|Conjure Blade}} can be targeted by {{C|Recycle}} to double the current {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy'''.\n* It will not count as a 0-cost card for {{C|Scrape}} or {{C|All for One}}.\n\n{{Clear}}\n== Expunger ==\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Expunger\n|Image       = Colorless-Expunger.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Special\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (9;15) damage X times.\n}}\n{{C|Expunger}} is a 1 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Special|Special}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 9 (15 if upgraded) damage X times. \n\nUniquely, X is not decided by the {{Icon|CE}} '''Energy''' you have when this card is played, but by the {{Icon|CE}} '''Energy''' you had when the {{C|Conjure Blade}} that created this was played. This means that X is consistent per copy of {{C|Expunger}} from the moment it is created. If X is 0, this card does nothing. \n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2412":{"pageid":2412,"ns":0,"title":"Deus Ex Machina","revisions":[{"revid":50699,"parentid":50697,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Deus Ex Machina\n|Image       = Purple-DeusExMachina.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = -2\n|Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}. <br>When you draw this card, add (2;3) {{C|Miracle|Miracles}} to your hand and {{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Draw, Hand\n}}\n{{Small Card Infobox|Miracle}}\n{{C|Deus Ex Machina}} is an unplayable {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. Whenever this card is drawn, add 2 (3 if upgraded) {{C|Miracle|Miracles}} to your hand. {{C|Deus Ex Machina}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* If you have played {{C|Master Reality}} before this card is activated, it will add upgraded {{C|Miracle|Miracles}} to your hand instead.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If a {{C|Miracle}} generated by this card exceeds your hand size limit, it gets added to the discard pile.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Deus Ex Machina}} has no effect unless actually drawn. This means its effect will not be triggered by:\n** Generating it in your hand, for example with {{R|Dead Branch}} or a {{P|Skill Potion}}.\n** Placing it into your hand, for example with {{C|Secret Technique}} or {{P|Liquid Memories}}.\n** Playing it, for example with {{C|Omniscience}} or {{C|Havoc}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n\n* A Deus Ex Machina is a plot device in which a seemingly unsolvable problem in a story is suddenly or abruptly resolved by an unexpected and unlikely occurrence.<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deus_ex_machina</ref>\n<references />\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2048":{"pageid":2048,"ns":0,"title":"Distraction","revisions":[{"revid":55417,"parentid":50503,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Distraction\n|Image       = Green-Distraction.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|CostPlus    = 0\n|Description = Add a random Skill into your hand.<br>It costs 0 this turn.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Distraction}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It will generate a random {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} card, which will have its normal cost replaced by 0 for this turn. {{C|Distraction}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself. X-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} cards generated this way will still consume all your energy. \n\n{{C|Distraction}} can only generate cards you can find in card rewards through character choice or custom run modifiers, and is not affected by {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* Some {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} cards cannot be generated, as they have some permanent effect out of combat, or can only be obtained from another source.\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Alchemize}}\n* {{C|Wish}}\n* {{C|Bandage Up}}\n* {{C|Apparition}}\n* {{C|J.A.X.}}\n* {{C|Beta}}\n* {{C|Insight}}\n* {{C|Miracle}}\n* {{C|Safety}}\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** All sources of random temporary card generation in combat (like  Dead Branch) can no longer generate cards that provide healing.\n** New tip added to indicate that healing cards cannot be generated randomly during combat.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2265":{"pageid":2265,"ns":0,"title":"Echo Form","revisions":[{"revid":55754,"parentid":50619,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Echo Form\n|Image       = Blue-EchoForm.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 3\n|Description = ({{KW|Ethereal}}. <br>;)The first card you play each turn is played twice.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Echo Form}} {{Keyword Infobox|Ethereal}}\n{{C|Echo Form}} is a 3 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It will give one {{BD|Echo Form}}, which will make the first card of your turn play twice. Unless upgraded, it has {{KW|Ethereal}}, which means it will {{KW|Exhaust}} if it is in your hand when you end your turn.\n\nX amount of {{BD|Echo Form}} will make the first X cards of your turn play twice. If the first play of a card doubled this way kills its target, it will not count towards that X. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Playing an {{C|Echo Form}} as the first card of a turn where you have an {{BD|Echo Form}} will result in you getting 3 {{BD|Echo Form}} total, meaning the next 2 cards you play will both be doubled.\n\n* Cards that scale upon being played, such as {{C|Claw}} and {{C|Genetic Algorithm}} will scale twice if doubled by {{BD|Echo Form}}.\n\n* Cards with {{KW|Fatal}} effects, such as {{C|Ritual Dagger}}, will trigger their {{KW|Fatal}} effect even if only the second play was {{KW|Fatal}}.\n\n* The second play of an X-cost card will use the same value of X as the first.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Other doubling effects, such as from {{C|Amplify}}, do not apply to the second play of a card doubled with {{BD|Echo Form}}. \n** For example, if you have two {{BD|Amplify}} and play a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} card with an {{BD|Echo Form}} active, that card will be played three times: once normally, which gets doubled by the first {{BD|Amplify}}, and once through {{BD|Echo Form}}, which will not get doubled by the second {{BD|Amplify}}.\n\n* The card played by {{C|Mayhem}} will be doubled by the first stack of {{BD|Echo Form}}, and consume that first stack.\n\n* The second play of a card doubled by {{BD|Echo Form}} counts as a card played.\n** It will activate or increase the counter of relics triggered by that card, such as {{R|Velvet Choker}}, {{R|Ink Bottle}}, {{R|Letter Opener}} or {{R|Bird-Faced Urn}}. \n** It will count towards relevant effects, such as {{BD|Beat of Death}}, The Awakened One's {{BD|Curiosity}}, {{BD|Hex}} or {{BD|Rage}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Using {{R|Blue Candle}} to {{KW|Exhaust}} a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} or {{R|Medical Kit}} to {{KW|Exhaust}} a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} will cause it to be doubled by the first stack of {{BD|Echo Form}}, and consume that first stack. In the case of {{R|Blue Candle}}, this will also cause you to lose 1 HP twice instead of only once.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Fix for proper behavior when duplicating cards like Rampage and Genetic Algorithm with effects like Echo Form.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 28: The Ritual'''\n** Fixed issue where cards stayed after combat with Echo Form or Double Tap.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2445":{"pageid":2445,"ns":0,"title":"Enlightenment","revisions":[{"revid":50724,"parentid":36925,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Enlightenment\n|Image       = Colorless-Enlightenment.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Reduce the cost of all cards in your hand to 1 this (turn;combat).\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{C|Enlightenment}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It reduces the cost of all cards that are in your hand and cost more than 1 '''Energy''' to 1 '''Energy''' for this turn, or for the rest of combat if {{C|Enlightenment}} is upgraded.\n\n== Obtaining Enlightenment ==\n{{C|Enlightenment}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* Cards that are reduced to a cost of 1 for the rest of combat by an upgraded {{C|Enlightenment}} will be randomized as normal by {{R|Snecko Eye}} and {{P|Snecko Oil}}, meaning the randomization will override {{C|Enlightenment}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Fixed Enlightenment+ not reducing cost of cards with 1 or 0 cost for turn.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 45: Impatience'''\n** Fixes for how Eviscerate incorrectly worked with cost reduction effects like Enlightenment.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 37: Darkness'''\n** Enlightenment card is now Uncommon (was Rare).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 9: Ascension'''\n** Fixed interaction of Enlightenment + Eviscerate + Discard.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** Enlightment+. This turn -> this combat.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1937":{"pageid":1937,"ns":0,"title":"Evolve","revisions":[{"revid":56762,"parentid":55769,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Evolve\n| Image       = Red-Evolve.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Whenever you draw a {{QueryLink|Cards|type|Status|Status}} card, draw (1;2) (card;cards).\n| GivesToPlayer = Evolve\n| PowerGives = Draw\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Evolve\n| Image        = Icon Evolve.png\n| Description  = Whenever you draw a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} card, draw X cards.\n| Type         = Buff\n| Stacks       = Intensity\n| BetweenTurns = \n| Cap          = \n| GivesToPlayer = Draw\n}}\n{{C|Evolve}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 1 (2 if upgraded) {{BD|Evolve}}, which draws that amount of cards whenever a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} card is drawn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{C|Evolve}} only activates upon {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} cards being drawn. This means that cards created in hand, such as through {{C|Power Through}}, do not trigger it. \n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 18: Paranormal'''\n** Evolve rework: No longer gives Wounds. Now triggers on any Status card, not just Wounds.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 4: Full speed ahead!'''\n** Evolve should no longer trigger even if No Draw power is active.\n\n* '''Day 1 Patch'''\n** Evolve power tooltip was displaying duplicate information incorrectly.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1857":{"pageid":1857,"ns":0,"title":"Havoc","revisions":[{"revid":56402,"parentid":55813,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Havoc\n| Image       = Red-Havoc.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 1\n| CostPlus    = 0\n| Description = Play the top card of your draw pile and {{KW|Exhaust}} it.\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Havoc}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It plays and {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} the top card of your draw pile, without expending any {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy'''. X-cost cards will use your current {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''' for X, without consuming that {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy'''.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* The top card being played and being {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} are separate, meaning the resolution of the played card takes place ''before'' any results of {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausting}} that card can occur.\n** This means that {{BD|Beat of Death}} will trigger ''before'' {{C|Feel No Pain}} gives {{KW|Block}} as a result of the card being {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} by {{C|Havoc}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Headbutt}}, {{C|Warcry}} and {{C|Thinking Ahead}} let you manipulate the top card of your draw pile, giving you more control over {{C|Havoc}}.\n* {{R|Frozen Eye}} allows you to see which card {{C|Havoc}} will target.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If your draw pile is empty when playing {{C|Havoc}}, it will shuffle your discard pile into your draw pile and target the new top card.\n* {{R|Strange Spoon}} has a 50% chance of saving a card that would be {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} by {{C|Havoc}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Fixed Mayhem, Havoc, Distilled Chaos, and Omniscience sometimes not playing cards if original target is dead.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 54: Loop'''\n** Tingsha, Sword Boomerang, Bouncing Flask, Rip and Tear, Thunder Orbs, Havoc, and Juggernaut now utilize seeded enemy target randomization.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Accuracy power now correctly works with Shivs played from the top of the deck via cards like Mayhem or Havoc.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 35: Aggregate'''\n** Fix for crash when playing Havoc against half dead enemies (Darkling/Awakened one).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 33: Terror'''\n** Havoc card now utilizes RNG to select its random target (save/load consistency).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 23: Testing Continues'''\n** Havoc card's description: Exhaust was not capitalized.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Havoc can now be played even when no cards are in your deck. (Discard will shuffle in)\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1527":{"pageid":1527,"ns":0,"title":"Heavy Blade","revisions":[{"revid":56352,"parentid":55816,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Heavy Blade\n| Image       = Red-HeavyBlade.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 2\n| Description = Deal 14 damage.<br>{{BD|Strength}} affects this card (3;5) times.\n| InteractsWith = Strength\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Strength}}\n{{C|Heavy Blade}} is a 2 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 14 damage, with 3 (5 if upgraded) additional damage times the amount {{BD|Strength}} you have, instead of just 1 additional damage for every {{BD|Strength}}.  \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes well with sources of {{BD|Strength}}:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Flex}}, {{C|Inflame}}, {{C|Rupture}}, {{C|Spot Weakness}}, {{C|Demon Form}}, {{C|Limit Break}}\n* {{C|J.A.X.}}\n* {{C|Reprogram}}\n* {{C|Fasting}}, {{C|Wish}}\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Brimstone}}, {{R|Du-Vu Doll}}, {{R|Girya}}, {{R|Mutagenic Strength}}, {{R|Red Skull}}, {{R|Shuriken}}, {{R|Sling of Courage}}, {{R|Vajra}}\n\n==== c) Potions ====\n* {{P|Flex Potion}}, {{P|Strength Potion}}, {{P|Cultist Potion}}\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* This card is also multiplicately affected by negative {{BD|Strength}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 31: Custom Mode'''\n** Optional UPGRADE_DESCRIPTION added for Pummel, Heavy Blade, Offering, and Reprogram\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 4: Full speed ahead!'''\n** Fixed rare crash for Heavy Blade.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2136":{"pageid":2136,"ns":0,"title":"Hello World","revisions":[{"revid":55818,"parentid":50595,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Hello World\n|Image       = Blue-HelloWorld.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = (;{{KW|Innate}}. <br>)At the start of your turn, add a random Common card into your hand.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Hello}}\n{{C|Hello World}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives one {{BD|Hello}}, which adds one random {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} card to your hand at the start of every turn. If upgraded, it has {{KW|Innate}}, meaning it will always appear in your first hand of combat.\n\n{{BD|Hello}} can only generate cards you can find in card rewards through character choice or custom run modifiers, and is not affected by {{R|Prismatic Shard}}. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{BD|Hello}} takes effect ''before'' your cards are drawn. This means that having a high amount of {{BD|Hello}} can cause you to draw less cards at the start of your turn due to the hand size limit.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If a {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} card generated by this card exceeds your hand size limit, it gets added to the discard pile.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The name of this card is a reference to a string of characters, \"Hello World\", which is often used as a demonstration in programming.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2072":{"pageid":2072,"ns":0,"title":"Hologram","revisions":[{"revid":54002,"parentid":53998,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Hologram\n|Image       = Blue-Hologram.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Gain (3;5) {{KW|Block}}.<br>Put a card from your discard pile into your hand.(<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.;)\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{C|Hologram}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* It can be used to place cards in hand, which does not activate any \"When drawn\" effects. For example, a {{C|Void}} in the discard pile generated by {{C|TURBO}} can be put into your hand using {{C|Hologram}} without losing {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' as a result of the {{C|Void}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The beta art of Hologram is a reference to the Spider-Man pointing at Spider-Man meme<ref>https://knowyourmeme.com/memes/spider-man-pointing-at-spider-man</ref>, original from a chapter of the Classic Spider-Man animated series.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Refactored Hologram card to not have to verify number of cards in the card itself.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1888":{"pageid":1888,"ns":0,"title":"Necronomicurse","revisions":[{"revid":56423,"parentid":55868,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Necronomicurse\n| Image       = Curse-Necronomicurse.png\n| Color       = Colorless\n| Type        = Curse\n| Cost        = -2\n| NoUpgrade   = true\n| Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}.<br>There is no escape from this curse.\n| GivesToPlayer = Unplayable\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Unplayable}}\n{{Small Relic Infobox|Necronomicon}}\n{{C|Necronomicurse}} is an {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} Card. It cannot be '''removed''' from your deck or {{KW|Transform|Transformed}} by any means. Moreover, unlike {{C|Ascender's Bane}} and {{C|Curse of the Bell}}, it cannot be {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} mid-combat either; doing so will immediately conjure another copy of the '''Curse''' into your hand.\n\n== Obtaining Necronomicurse ==\n'''Necronomicurse''' is obtained when you pick up {{R|Necronomicon|The Necronomicon}} from the {{E|Cursed Tome}} event.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* When {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}, '''Necronomicurse''' returns to your hand ''after'' {{KW|Exhaust}} triggers happen.\n** If your hand is full and you have {{R|Dead Branch}} or {{C|Dark Embrace}} in play, '''Necronomicurse''' will be unable to be added to your hand, as it is full again, and will go to your '''Discard Pile''' instead.\n\n=== Synergies ===\nAs '''Necronomicurse''' is a '''{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}''', it interacts with the following:\n* {{C|Fire Breathing}} will deal '''6(10)''' damage when it is drawn.\n* {{R|Du-Vu Doll}} will give you '''+1''' {{BD|Strength}} each combat.\n* {{R|Blue Candle}} can be used to {{KW|Exhaust}} it for '''1 HP'''. \n* When added to the deck, it will be negated by {{R|Omamori}}, or gain you '''6 max HP''' if you have {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} and ''not'' Omamori.\nIn addition, '''Necronomicurse''' can be {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} repeatedly, allowing cards such as {{C|Burning Pact}}, {{C|Sever Soul}}, and {{C|Second Wind}} to use it for value repeatedly.\n\n=== Infinite ===\nDue to '''Necronomicurse''''s unique ability to {{KW|Exhaust}} repeatedly, it can be used in some unusual '''infinites'''. \n\nIf you have {{R|Blue Candle}} and {{R|Tungsten Rod}}, then you may play '''Necronomicurse''' an unlimited number of times. On its own, this doesn't accomplish anything, but there are ways to get value from it:\n* You have unlimited card plays to trigger {{C|After Image}}, {{C|A Thousand Cuts}}, or {{R|Ink Bottle}}.\n* You have unlimited {{KW|Exhaust}} triggers for {{C|Feel No Pain}}, {{C|Dark Embrace}}, or {{R|Charon's Ashes}}.\nLate in [[Custom Mode#Endless|Endless]] runs, the addition of the [[Blight]] {{R|Time Maze}} prevents you from playing more than '''15''' ''non-Curse'' cards in one turn. The intent of the '''Blight''' appears to be to remove '''infinite''' combos as an option, while not penalizing the player for {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausting}} {{C|Pride}}. However, due to this exception to the rule, the above '''infinites''' eventually become the ''only'' viable '''infinites''' in [[Custom Mode#Endless|Endless Mode]].\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{C|Clash}} can only be played when all cards in your hand are {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, if it is drawn at the same time as '''Necronomicurse''', it cannot be played.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* At the event {{E|N'loth}}, offering '''N'loth''' {{R|Necronomicon}} will remove exactly 1 copy of '''Necronomicurse'''. If the '''Curse''' was duplicated by {{E|Duplicator}} or {{R|Dolly's Mirror}}, you keep the other copies.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2076":{"pageid":2076,"ns":0,"title":"Steam Barrier","revisions":[{"revid":55957,"parentid":50568,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Steam Barrier\n|Image       = Blue-SteamBarrier.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Gain (6;8) {{KW|Block}}. Decrease this card's {{KW|Block}} by 1 this combat.\n}}\n{{C|Steam Barrier}} is a 0 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{C|Steam Barrier}} will not decrease its base {{KW|Block}} but its total {{KW|Block}}, meaning any increase from {{BD|Dexterity}} will also be removed over time by playing this card.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* In the game code, Steam Barrier is called Steam.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2298":{"pageid":2298,"ns":0,"title":"Swivel","revisions":[{"revid":55966,"parentid":50683,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Swivel\n|Image       = Purple-Swivel.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Gain (8;11) {{KW|Block}}. <br>The next Attack you play costs 0.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Free Attack Power}}{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Swivel}} is a 2 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 8 (11 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}} and 1 {{BD|Free Attack Power}}, which allows you to ignore the {{Icon|PE}}-cost of the next {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card you play. X costs {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards will be played for your current {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' without spending it. Playing any  {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} will consume one {{BD|Free Attack Power}}, even if it already costed 0.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* As it only ignores the {{Icon|PE}}-cost of the next {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card and does not actually change the actual cost of any cards, it has no synergy with things like {{C|All for One}} or {{R|Wrist Blade}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2480":{"pageid":2480,"ns":0,"title":"The Bomb","revisions":[{"revid":55974,"parentid":50750,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = The Bomb\n|Image       = Colorless-TheBomb.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = At the end of 3 turns, deal (40;50) damage to ALL enemies.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|The Bomb}}\n{{C|The Bomb}} is a 2 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives one stack of {{BD|The Bomb}}, which has a counter of 3 that goes down by 1 at the end of every turn, dealing 40 (50 if upgraded) damage to '''ALL''' enemies when reaching 0. \n\nPlaying {{C|The Bomb}} multiple times will give a separate single stack of {{BD|The Bomb}} each time.\n\n== Obtaining The Bomb ==\n{{C|The Bomb}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]], [[Elites]] and [[Bosses]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a negative effect.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n{{BD|The Bomb}} activates before the enemy turn. On top of happening before enemy intents, it will also activate before:\n* Before {{BD|Invincible}} resets\n* Before {{BD|Poison}} activates\n\nWhen alongside other [[Buffs]] or [[Debuffs]] which activate at the end of the player's turn, {{BD|The Bomb}} activates in the order the buffs were gained. This includes:\n* {{BD|Regen}}\n* {{BD|Constricted}}\n* {{BD|Combust}}\n* {{BD|Omega}}\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* This damage is not affected by {{BD|Vulnerable}}, {{BD|Strength}}, or {{BD|Double Damage}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 55: Blur'''\n** The Bomb card damage buffed from 30 -> 40.\n** The Bomb+ card damage buffed from 40 -> 50.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** The Bomb+ card buff: 36 -> 40 damage.\n** The Bomb card's buff icon now correctly displays numbers in blue.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 38: Bane'''\n** Adding colorless card The Bomb.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2285":{"pageid":2285,"ns":0,"title":"Third Eye","revisions":[{"revid":50653,"parentid":36376,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Third Eye\n|Image       = Purple-ThirdEye.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Gain (7;9) {{KW|Block}}. <br>{{KW|Scry}} (3;5).\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}} {{Keyword Infobox|Scry}}\n{{C|Third Eye}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 7 (9 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}, and allows you to {{KW|Scry}} 3 (5 if upgraded) cards.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* If you have {{R|Golden Eye}}, you will be able to {{KW|Scry}} 2 more cards.\n* Playing {{C|Third Eye}} will activate {{C|Nirvana}}.\n* As it allows you to {{KW|Scry}}, any {{C|Weave}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand. \n** If a {{C|Weave}} is among the cards {{KW|Scry|Scryed}} by {{C|Third Eye}} and is discarded this way, it will immediately be brought back into your hand.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}